<title>HONDURAS: Latin coffee cooperatives to meet in Honduras.</title>
<headline>Latin coffee cooperatives to meet in Honduras.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Representatives of Latin American and Caribbean coffee cooperatives and federations meet next week in Honduras to set up a region-wide interest association, an official said Friday.</p>
<p>Luis Cuellar, delegate for the International Copperative Alliance, said the meeting with start Monday in the town of Santa Rose de Copan. Representatives will move on to Costa Rica mid-week and end the gathering May 23.</p>
<p>The top aim will be to establish a region wide group called the Latin American Association of Coffee Growing Cooperatives.</p>
<p>Cuellar said representatives from Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, Costa Rica, Dominican Republic, Mexico, Nicaragua, El Salvador, Panama and Honduras will attend.</p>
<p>Other incentives will be to create a network of information exchange and the gathering will attempt to work out mechanisms to create a process of technical integration and cooperation.</p>
<p>((Honduras bureau +504 392885))</p>
